{{also|Grenade|grénade}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{borrowing|fr|grenade}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|grenate|lang=fro}} in the phrase {{term|pome grenate||pomegranate|lang=fro}}, ultimately from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|pomum granatum||seeded fruit|lang=la}}. The ''-d'' developed in French under influence of Spanish {{term|granada|lang=es}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡɹəˈneɪd/}}
* {{rhymes|eɪd}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{obsolete}} A [[pomegranate]].
# A small [[explosive]] [[device]], designed to be thrown by hand or launched from a grenade launcher.

